wider audience."}, {"sourceSlug": "pierre-sylvain-rgis", "sourceName": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "debate-on-spinozism", "targetName": "Debate on Spinozism", "context": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis was a prominent participant in the intellectual debates surrounding Baruch Spinoza's philosophy, particularly critiquing his determinism."}, {"sourceSlug": "pierre-sylvain-rgis", "sourceName": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "french-academy-of-sciences", "targetName": "French Academy of Sciences", "context": "Régis's philosophical contributions and reputation led to his nomination as an associate member of the French Academy of Sciences in 1699."}], "places": [{"name": "Agen, France", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Primary Residence & Work"}, {"name": "French Kingdom", "role": "Sphere of Influence"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Pierre-Sylvain Régis", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "pierre-sylvain-régis"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3507055", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pierre-Sylvain_R%C3%A9gis"], "tags": ["France", "Philosophers & Thinkers", "Europe", "doctrine-development", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis left a notable mark on Early Modern history, documented across 0 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed philosophical ideas to ongoing intellectual discourse; Contributed to global exchange networks, modern state formation, and scientific revolution. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis significantly impacted French intellectual life by systematizing and popularizing Cartesian philosophy through his comprehensive *Cours entier de philosophie*, thereby shaping the reception of rationalism and contributing to the critical discourse against Spinozism.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-25T00:25:41Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#32793077860", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Pierre Sylvain Régis was a French Cartesian philosopher and a prominent critic of Spinoza. Known as a philosopher, he was nominated to the French Academy of Sciences in 1699.", "newValue": "Pierre-Sylvain Régis (1632–1707) was a pivotal French Cartesian philosopher whose intellectual contributions significantly shaped the reception and dissemination of René Descartes's ideas in late 17th-century France. Born in Agen, he emerged as a leading proponent of rationalism, meticulously systematizing Cartesian philosophy and engaging directly with its critics and contemporaries. His work provided a comprehensive, accessible framework for understanding Descartes, making him a central figure in the intellectual currents of the Early Modern era.

Régis's magnum opus, the three-volume *Cours entier de philosophie ou Système général selon les principes de M. Descartes* (1690), served as an authoritative exposition of Cartesian thought, covering metaphysics, physics, and ethics. He actively participated in the vibrant philosophical debates of his time, famously challenging the pantheistic implications of Baruch Spinoza's *Ethics* and engaging in discussions with Nicolas Malebranche regarding the nature of ideas and divine causality. His rigorous defense of Cartesian principles against various philosophical adversaries solidified his reputation, culminating in his nomination to the French Academy of Sciences in 1699, a testament to his intellectual stature.

The legacy of Pierre-Sylvain Régis is multifaceted: he not only clarified and popularized Cartesianism for a wider French audience but also contributed to defining the parameters of rationalist discourse. His detailed critiques of Spinoza's determinism and his systematic approach to philosophy influenced subsequent generations of thinkers who grappled with the implications of modern philosophy. By distilling complex ideas into an organized system, Régis played a crucial role in the intellectual transition from the scholastic tradition to the Enlightenment's emphasis on reason and systematic inquiry."}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-25T00:25:41Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#32793077860", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Early Modern era: age of exploration, printing revolution, and religious reformation", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1632, Agen"}, {"title": "Ongoing philosophical inquiry and intellectual debate", "type": "Idea", "year": "1632, Agen"}], "newValue": ["The intellectual ferment of 17th-century France, marked by the decline of scholasticism and the rise of new philosophical systems, created fertile ground for Régis's work.", "The profound influence and widespread interest in René Descartes's philosophy provided Régis with a foundational framework and a compelling subject for his systematic expositions.", "His rigorous education and early exposure to the burgeoning rationalist movement in Paris equipped him with the tools and motivation to become a leading Cartesian proponent."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-25T00:25:41Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#32793077860", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Contributed philosophical ideas to ongoing intellectual discourse", "type": "Idea", "year": "1707-01-11"}, {"title": "Contributed to global exchange networks, modern state formation, and scientific revolution", "type": "Movement", "year": "1707-01-11"}], "newValue": ["Pierre-Sylvain Régis's systematic publ